    escalation: 'Apps SIN SCIM (solo administración manual): el alta manual queda documentada como deuda con revisión trimestral reforzada (RB-IAM-015) y alerta al líder de IAM si la población crece. Errores persistentes de provisioning (401/403 del endpoint, mapeos que fallan): soporte del proveedor con el error textual de ProvisioningLogs; riesgo de licencias fuera de control: gestor de licencias/compras.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, access to the new SaaS application under ticket {{TICKET_ID}} has been provisioned for the approved user group. Users sign in with their corporate identity through single sign-on, and account creation and updates are now automated from our directory; when someone leaves the company, their application access is removed automatically. The initial provisioning results and a full lifecycle test, including access removal, were verified before closing the ticket. The application owner is recorded in our application inventory for quarterly access review.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'SaaS application onboarding at {{TIMESTAMP}}: app added from the Entra gallery to tenant {{TENANT}}, SSO configured first (SAML per the SSO runbook or OIDC via gallery), and SCIM provisioning enabled in Automatic mode with the vendor endpoint and secret token (connection test passed). Provisioning scope limited to the target group with attribute mappings reviewed. Initial cycle completed and validated in ProvisioningLogs (Create/Update actions with Success status); full lifecycle test performed including group-removal-driven deactivation for a test account, guaranteeing leaver propagation. App recorded in the application inventory with owner and next review date.',
    keywords: ['saas', 'scim', 'provisioning', 'aprovisionamiento', 'provisioninglogs', 'enterprise application', 'galeria', 'gallery app', 'deprovisioning', 'ciclo de vida', 'licencias', 'dueno de app', 'app owner', 'entra', 'single sign-on', 'automatic provisioning', 'scope'],
